As a general rule I consider the fetishisation of permission for
distribution of something like this - that I put up with the express aim
that anyone in the world could get it - quite absurd. Nice if they'd put
my name on it, though, but I gather from email that they have.

>>"You generally do not want to come back after entering Gehennom. I got a
>>lot of criticism for saying that, but I am trying to emphasize the need for
>>thorough preparation at this point."
>The guide is correct here.  If, after using everything from the main 
>dungeon, the mines, the Castle, the Valley, and the Quest, the player 
>doesn't have the AK, (1) he's been badly wasteful or astonishingly 
>unlucky (hint: probably the former) and (2) slogging through the mazes 
>with -12 AC (or whatever) is not likely to fix things.

First ascensions often _are_ wasteful. Now that shouldn't be a model, but
the fact is that someone trying for one will very likely reach Gehennom
with a shortage of things like SoRC and holy water that a more
conservative player will have a vast surplus of. Why not haul any that one
finds in Gehennom back to the stash?

I'm to a degree assuming controlled levelport here, which a strategy guide
ought to recommend very strongly. With controlled levelport the cost of a
return to one's stash is basically zero. Also remember that a
first-ascender will be prone to packrattery; emphasising that you don't
have to carry it all with you is very important.

>The goal of the game is to ascend, not to Haul Stuff Long Distances.  
>Collecting Stuff helps with the goal, but eventually runs into 
>diminishing returns.  

But I think expending the very small effort of a controlled levelport for
the significant gain of a stash-rearrangement immediately before Rodney is
dead (ie, no time pressure) and being able to leave care packages on DL 1
and in other places is obviously a worthwhile return.

>>the first maze level in Gehennom isn't somehow magic compared with the
>>maze levels that very likely appeared below Medusa,
>I always dig straight down through the Medusa mazes.  Why would you do 
>anything else?

That's up to you. But what's the difference between the first Gehennom
maze and a Medusa maze?
